<%#
  A stretch of this file that the pull request did not touch, folded away so a
  small edit in a long document is not buried in the document.

  A native <details>, so it opens with JavaScript off and the blocks inside it
  are ordinary DOM the whole time: every id resolves, every gutter "+" works
  the moment the run is open, and nothing is fetched to reveal it. The
  `collapse` controller only swaps the word Show for Hide.

  The blocks are direct children of the <details> rather than wrapped in a
  container, because `.md-block` is its own two-column grid and a wrapper
  would put the revealed blocks' gutters out of line with the rest of the
  document.

  Review::CollapsedRuns decides what lands here. Nothing carrying a comment
  ever does.

  Locals: segment (Review::CollapsedRuns::Segment), pull_request,
          page (Review::Page)
%>
<details class="md-run" data-controller="collapse" data-testid="unchanged-run">
  <summary class="md-run-summary">
    <span><%= count_of(segment.size, "unchanged block") %></span>
    <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
    <span data-collapse-target="label">Show</span>
  </summary>

  <% segment.blocks.each do |annotated| %>
    <%= render "block", annotated: annotated, pull_request: pull_request, page: page %>
  <% end %>
</details>
